session Relative_Arbitrage = Path_Space_Operations +
  description "
    Theorem 1.1 of Lai, Shkolnikov and Soner, Relative arbitrage problem under
    eigenvalue lower bounds (arXiv:2512.17702): the value function of the
    minimum-exit-time problem under eigenvalue constraints on the covariation
    is the unique bounded upper semicontinuous viscosity solution of the
    associated degenerate elliptic equation.

    The operator of Eq. (1.9), its envelopes, the subspace-tangential field
    and the comparison principle (Theorem 4.2(a)) are in the probability-free
    session Relative_Arbitrage_Equation; the operations on path laws (cutting,
    glueing, shifting, sampling at a stopping time) and the class of laws
    with constrained covariation, for an arbitrary constraint set, are in
    Path_Space_Operations.  This session instantiates that class at the
    eigenvalue constraint set of Eq. (1.7), proves the dynamic programming
    principle for it, and proves the five clauses for its value function.
  "
